WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:00.090
###SIGNS

00:01.940 --> 00:05.350
Even if the world ends up hiding in fear

00:05.350 --> 00:08.190
You mustn't let that get you down

00:08.190 --> 00:13.950
Spending your time like that isn't right

00:24.520 --> 00:27.390
Don’t run away, don’t let go

00:27.390 --> 00:30.200
Don’t stop, but stand right there

00:30.200 --> 00:35.870
And now say a few words that means something

00:35.870 --> 00:38.650
Face one another and meet half way

00:38.650 --> 00:41.470
Talk things out, love one another

00:41.470 --> 00:47.900
You need to stop beating around the bush

00:47.900 --> 00:53.400
If you’re in pain, don’t just try to bear it

00:53.400 --> 00:58.450
You gotta move forward before it tears you apart

00:58.450 --> 01:01.740
Sing! Dance! Flee! Tracy!

01:01.740 --> 01:04.560
We're idols with too many secrets

01:04.560 --> 01:09.920
So we're saying goodbye to the real world

01:09.920 --> 01:13.130
So just keep waiting

01:13.130 --> 01:15.860
until we make our return

01:15.860 --> 01:18.320
Hide those tears

01:18.320 --> 01:19.550
Exodus!

01:30.980 --> 01:33.980
Episode 1

01:30.980 --> 01:33.980
Escape Tokyo

01:37.990 --> 01:39.680
Aya-chan, Akane-chan!

01:39.680 --> 01:43.490
Wasn't I amazing out there today?

01:43.490 --> 01:47.360
I even pulled off that part of the chorus I've been having trouble with!

01:47.360 --> 01:48.330
That you did.

01:48.330 --> 01:50.850
I have a good feeling about today.

01:50.850 --> 01:53.840
We even got separate rooms to change in for the first time!

01:53.840 --> 01:57.840
My, and the costumes the organizers gave us are just adorable.

01:58.450 --> 02:01.050
Let's give it our all during the sales event at noon, too!

02:01.050 --> 02:05.010
We finally have the chance to meet our fans firsthand!

02:05.010 --> 02:05.890
Right.

02:05.890 --> 02:07.510
Hey, Alpine.

02:07.510 --> 02:08.870
What is it, Akane-chan?

02:08.870 --> 02:11.320
I see where you're coming from,

02:11.320 --> 02:12.730
but face reality!

02:12.730 --> 02:14.190
We're sitting on toilets!

02:14.190 --> 02:16.360
They stuck us in bathroom stalls!

02:16.360 --> 02:19.190
We're selling food samples for a store!

02:19.190 --> 02:20.820
Don't put it like that!

02:20.820 --> 02:23.450
Just let me dream a little...

02:23.450 --> 02:27.980
We don't have the time to daydream.

02:27.980 --> 02:30.940
Reality is calling us, and we have to face it!

02:30.940 --> 02:36.090
My grandfather always said that living in your own fantasies never solves anything.

02:36.090 --> 02:38.090
That self-proclaimed Kappa?

02:38.090 --> 02:40.570
No, he really is a Kappa!

02:40.570 --> 02:41.970
That's amazing!

02:41.970 --> 02:44.920
I've never heard of a Kappa that thinks realistically!

02:44.920 --> 02:48.320
Grandfather was the most
pragmatic man in our village.

02:48.320 --> 02:49.600
Despite being a Kappa?

02:49.600 --> 02:50.560
Yeah.

02:51.070 --> 02:52.480
Oh, god...

02:52.480 --> 02:56.920
Could they make these costume any <i>more</i> revealing?

02:56.920 --> 02:59.430
Even our stage costumes cover more.

02:59.430 --> 03:01.390
This skirt won't sit down!

03:01.390 --> 03:03.940
It's hiding everything, right?

03:03.940 --> 03:06.200
This outfit is certainly embarrassing.

03:06.200 --> 03:09.870
And what's up with these knives?

03:09.870 --> 03:14.360
We're selling samples of ham and sausages, remember?

03:14.360 --> 03:17.240
I bet middle schoolers fantasize about wearing this stuff.

03:17.240 --> 03:19.390
Life itself is a middle schooler's fantasy.

03:19.390 --> 03:21.340
I guess that makes the costumes perfect, huh?

03:23.110 --> 03:25.050
I'm sorry, girls.

03:25.050 --> 03:27.850
Wh-Why are <i>you</i> apologizing?

03:27.850 --> 03:31.680
I mean, I'm supposed to be the leader after all.

03:31.680 --> 03:37.220
Maybe Taguchi-san keeps giving us these oddball jobs because I'm unreliable.

03:37.220 --> 03:39.320
That man doesn't deserve our respect.

03:39.320 --> 03:41.320
He wasn't even there for our performance earlier.

03:41.320 --> 03:45.320
He manages Ginger as well, so I'm sure he's just busy.

03:45.320 --> 03:47.240
So it's okay for him to put them above us?

03:49.150 --> 03:50.370
Hey, Aya...

03:50.650 --> 03:53.140
How many views has our PV gotten?

03:55.080 --> 03:58.550
"Tracy" New Song PV

03:55.080 --> 03:58.550
Tracy's Official Channel

03:55.550 --> 03:58.550
Only 125. Same as yesterday.

03:58.550 --> 04:00.520
How many Tweeter followers do we have?

04:00.520 --> 04:01.720
58.

04:01.720 --> 04:03.230
Down three from yesterday.

04:04.890 --> 04:06.640
We have the same manager,

04:06.930 --> 04:11.560
but Ginger's super famous!
They've got a million views and 500,000 followers.

04:11.560 --> 04:14.580
Compared to them, we're nothing but super <i>salesgirls</i>.

04:14.580 --> 04:16.520
Talk about depressing...

04:16.750 --> 04:17.630
Uh...

04:17.630 --> 04:21.980
C-Come on, you know what they say, "great talent blooms late," and all!

04:21.980 --> 04:24.360
But aren't idols supposed to be young buds?

04:26.640 --> 04:28.340
I'm getting a call on Skyype.

04:28.340 --> 04:30.640
Is it Onee-san?

04:34.720 --> 04:36.880
Good morning, Team Tracy.

04:36.880 --> 04:38.540
Good morning!

04:38.540 --> 04:40.600
Oh my, cute costumes you've got there.

04:40.600 --> 04:43.260
Uh, it's a long story...

04:43.260 --> 04:48.720
More importantly, did you watch the video we sent you earlier?

04:48.720 --> 04:51.860
Indeed. You were excellent on stage today.

04:51.860 --> 04:54.600
The three of you have really improved.

04:54.600 --> 04:56.200
You think so?!

04:56.200 --> 04:57.410
You bet.

04:57.410 --> 05:01.030
I intentionally made the choreography more difficult this time,

05:01.030 --> 05:03.920
but you three pulled it off perfectly.

05:03.920 --> 05:06.520
The part that especially stuck out was section B of the chorus.

05:06.520 --> 05:08.400
You had the timing spot on!

05:09.950 --> 05:12.840
But there's always room for improvement.

05:12.840 --> 05:14.160
I'm sure you know that, though.

05:14.520 --> 05:15.760
Right!

05:15.760 --> 05:19.210
How about we go over it from the beginning.

05:19.210 --> 05:20.250
First of all...

05:20.640 --> 05:22.910
No, wait! About that...

05:24.040 --> 05:25.340
Understood...

05:25.340 --> 05:31.140
Nation Wide
Concert
Tour

05:25.880 --> 05:28.620
Of course not! It's being prepared as we speak!

05:30.630 --> 05:32.740
I just need three more days!

05:32.740 --> 05:35.850
Three more days, and I <i>guarantee</i> everything will go smoothly.

05:35.850 --> 05:37.100
No.

05:38.320 --> 05:40.160
I can't wait any longer.

05:40.160 --> 05:42.020
Prepare yourself.

05:45.990 --> 05:48.400
I'm so beat!

05:48.400 --> 05:51.620
All that hard work's got my tummy growling.

05:51.620 --> 05:55.650
All right, girls! We know what we've gotta work on for the next performance!

05:55.650 --> 05:57.170
Let's practice a ton for it!

05:57.170 --> 05:58.000
Yeah!

05:58.000 --> 06:00.750
Not that there's anything for us to practice for right now...

06:02.360 --> 06:03.650
Oh, yeah...

06:03.650 --> 06:05.170
Good point.

06:05.170 --> 06:06.430
Try these!

06:07.260 --> 06:11.760
These pastries are really tasty, so try one!

06:15.960 --> 06:19.600
They look typical on the outside,
but the taste is really special, don't you think?

06:19.600 --> 06:24.340
Sure, they may not be famous,
but the store has its own little fanbase.

06:24.340 --> 06:27.320
So I'm sure it'll all work out for us too!

06:27.560 --> 06:31.700
Once you try these pastries you realize how great they really are.

06:35.410 --> 06:36.480
You're right.

06:36.480 --> 06:38.680
You can tell these were made with love.

06:38.680 --> 06:39.710
Exactly!

06:44.290 --> 06:45.250
I've decided!

06:48.560 --> 06:50.510
Chew before you swallow.

06:50.510 --> 06:52.760
Akane, what did you decide?

06:53.820 --> 06:57.030
Well, I was thinking...

06:57.030 --> 06:59.730
Ham doesn't sell itself, you know!

07:00.960 --> 07:04.060
At what point did our conversation inspire <i>that</i>?

07:04.060 --> 07:08.130
I was just thinking that if we went out there and gave it our all,

07:08.130 --> 07:10.710
the people out there will take notice!

07:10.710 --> 07:12.280
Maybe...

07:12.280 --> 07:14.270
They'll respect our marketing?

07:14.270 --> 07:16.280
That's, well...

07:17.460 --> 07:21.050
The little girls' room is calling me!
I'll be right back.

07:21.050 --> 07:22.960
You're already here.

07:22.960 --> 07:25.290
Actually, um...

07:25.290 --> 07:29.540
I-I'm parched! I'm gonna go get drinks.

07:40.300 --> 07:41.390
<i>I've decided!</i>

07:41.390 --> 07:43.120
<i>I can't let this continue.</i>

07:43.120 --> 07:46.150
<i>I'm going to talk to Taguchi-san face-to-face!</i>

07:55.410 --> 07:56.530
Excuse me?

07:57.490 --> 07:58.990
Yes, missy?

08:01.000 --> 08:03.900
"I've decided," she says.

08:03.900 --> 08:08.700
Do you think she wants to leave Tracy?

08:11.190 --> 08:13.010
Then there's not much we can do.

08:13.400 --> 08:17.960
Akane is the one that dragged us this far.

08:17.960 --> 08:19.980
If it wasn't for her,

08:19.980 --> 08:23.110
I'm sure I would have given up on being an idol long ago.

08:23.110 --> 08:24.230
Don't say that!

08:24.540 --> 08:27.050
You're an amazing idol!

08:27.050 --> 08:29.580
I'm the useless one.

08:30.550 --> 08:34.450
Akane is talented enough to fit into any group.

08:34.450 --> 08:38.250
So if Akane leaves,

08:38.250 --> 08:39.080
then I...

08:40.040 --> 08:41.430
Aya-chan...

08:44.440 --> 08:47.020
I need to use the restroom too!

08:47.020 --> 08:49.030
This <i>is</i> the restroom.

08:49.030 --> 08:51.610
Th-Then... I'll go buy juice!

08:51.610 --> 08:54.060
Akane just left to get drinks.

08:54.060 --> 08:57.280
Th-Th-Then I'll go buy salted kelp!

08:58.660 --> 09:00.680
Salted kelp?

09:03.760 --> 09:05.420
Akane-chan...

09:07.100 --> 09:09.060
What's wrong with you?

09:10.570 --> 09:13.690
U-Um, have you seen Taguchi-san...

09:13.690 --> 09:16.680
Our manager, I mean. Have you seen him?

09:16.680 --> 09:23.200
He's got a stern face like this, white teeth and dark skin.

09:23.200 --> 09:25.580
What a coincidence! Was another lass

09:25.580 --> 09:29.830
dressed just like you who asked me the same question.

09:29.830 --> 09:32.590
That young man must be mighty popular.

09:32.590 --> 09:34.960
You lot tryin' to woo 'im?

09:34.960 --> 09:36.800
N-Not at all!

09:37.240 --> 09:42.360
Saw the two near the storage room 'round the corner.

09:43.200 --> 09:45.190
Akane-chan?

09:45.190 --> 09:47.640
She'll get 'im first if you don't hurry, missy.

09:49.060 --> 09:53.020
Gosh, something must've
happened between 'em two.

09:53.020 --> 09:55.650
Anyway, thanks for your help.

10:20.830 --> 10:21.940
A cellphone?

10:23.480 --> 10:25.420
Did someone lose it?

10:43.680 --> 10:44.990
Taguchi-san...

10:45.290 --> 10:46.860
A prank...?

10:46.860 --> 10:48.620
O-Of course, a prank.

10:48.620 --> 10:49.870
It must be.

10:49.870 --> 10:54.460
But recording pranks on unpopular idols won't get you any views, you know...

11:18.520 --> 11:19.780
I've decided.

11:20.830 --> 11:22.720
Did Akane-chan...

11:22.720 --> 11:25.120
I heard someone scream. Are you all right, Alpine?

11:37.280 --> 11:38.460
No good.

11:38.460 --> 11:39.340
He's dead.

11:39.340 --> 11:41.300
So he's really...

11:45.510 --> 11:47.140
Let me see it.

11:50.390 --> 11:52.460
Did you touch the blade?

11:53.690 --> 11:54.900
You're kidding.

12:01.160 --> 12:02.750
Why would you do this, Aya?!

12:02.750 --> 12:05.400
Don't worry, Akane-chan! We won't tell anyone!

12:05.400 --> 12:07.120
Alpine did nothing wrong!

12:07.910 --> 12:09.160
Huh?

12:09.160 --> 12:11.140
Isn't the killer...

12:11.140 --> 12:12.600
Akane-chan?

12:11.140 --> 12:12.600
Alpine?

12:11.140 --> 12:12.600
Aya-chan?

12:12.600 --> 12:13.710
It wasn't her?

12:15.040 --> 12:17.500
A murder!

12:17.500 --> 12:19.420
Somebody! There's been a murder!

12:19.420 --> 12:22.920
The idol girls killed a man!

12:28.320 --> 12:30.680
I-In the storage room, hurry!

12:32.430 --> 12:34.640
Wh-Wh-What do we do?!

12:34.640 --> 12:35.500
I don't know...

12:35.500 --> 12:37.310
The guards are on their way.

12:37.310 --> 12:38.260
Wait!

12:38.260 --> 12:41.630
My grandfather always told me to stay calm in dire situations!

12:41.630 --> 12:44.420
More life lessons from the realist Kappa.

12:44.420 --> 12:46.740
He didn't pull the souls out of people's anuses for nothing!

12:46.740 --> 12:48.900
Let's take a deep breath and calm down.

12:48.900 --> 12:50.480
One, two...

12:57.200 --> 13:00.800
That didn't solve a thing!

13:01.040 --> 13:01.930
Who's phone?

13:01.930 --> 13:03.980
This sounds like one of Ginger's songs.

13:05.620 --> 13:08.180
Is that Taguchi-san's smartphone?

13:10.180 --> 13:11.650
I found it on the floor.

13:11.650 --> 13:12.850
Do we answer?

13:12.850 --> 13:14.850
Incoming call

13:12.850 --> 13:14.850
Anonymous call

13:17.630 --> 13:18.940
Hello?

13:18.940 --> 13:20.160
Who is this?

13:20.160 --> 13:22.910
Is that... you, Akane-chan?

13:22.910 --> 13:24.460
Why are you answering?

13:24.460 --> 13:26.000
Onee-san?

13:26.000 --> 13:27.370
Onee-san, help us!

13:27.370 --> 13:29.950
Taguchi-san is lying dead right in front of us!

13:29.950 --> 13:31.370
Murdered in all likelihood.

13:32.340 --> 13:33.960
You aren't mistaken, are you?

13:33.960 --> 13:34.870
No...

13:34.870 --> 13:37.100
Do you know who did it?

13:37.100 --> 13:38.970
Uh...

13:38.970 --> 13:41.710
Not us! That much is for sure.

13:41.920 --> 13:45.090
But the murder weapon is probably Akane's knife.

13:47.590 --> 13:52.000
And moreover, I was the one witnessed with it.

13:52.000 --> 13:53.920
Tell us what to do, Onee-san!

13:53.920 --> 13:56.360
Should we turn ourselves in?

13:56.360 --> 13:58.270
For a crime we didn't do?!

13:58.270 --> 14:00.400
I wouldn't recommend that route.

14:00.400 --> 14:04.640
With the decreasing arrest rates and all the false charges lately,

14:04.640 --> 14:07.280
the police and prosecutors might be too impulsive to trust.

14:07.770 --> 14:09.630
I suggest you find a way out for now.

14:09.630 --> 14:12.870
You'll have time to sit down and think all this through later.

14:12.870 --> 14:14.200
Um...

14:14.200 --> 14:15.370
You're saying...

14:15.370 --> 14:16.200
In other words...

14:16.870 --> 14:18.830
Make a run for it. Right now!

14:30.510 --> 14:33.010
Inspector Koigakubo,

14:33.010 --> 14:36.580
you fired 17 rounds. He was just a petty thief.

14:36.580 --> 14:37.600
Care to explain?

14:38.050 --> 14:42.060
That was standard procedure back in Johannesburg.

14:42.060 --> 14:44.160
Well, this is Japan!

14:44.160 --> 14:47.690
There has been report of a murder at the Musashino Mall.

14:47.940 --> 14:52.450
Finally, the time has come for I,
Koigakubo Miho, to shine!

14:52.450 --> 14:55.240
No, it hasn't! Come back here!

14:55.240 --> 14:57.450
Where are you going? Inspector Gakubo!

15:01.210 --> 15:03.170
Good thing this amusement park was nearby.

15:03.420 --> 15:06.130
Even our stage costumes fit in here.

15:06.130 --> 15:09.240
Jeez, we need to calm down!

15:09.240 --> 15:12.430
I can't believe all we grabbed was our stage costumes!

15:12.430 --> 15:15.680
But it's a good thing we're not popular.

15:15.680 --> 15:18.090
If it were Ginger, the crowd would be all over them.

15:18.090 --> 15:20.160
Quit making us sound so pitiful.

15:23.200 --> 15:24.810
The Musashino Dome.

15:24.810 --> 15:26.520
It's so big.

15:26.520 --> 15:27.360
Yeah.

15:30.870 --> 15:33.480
The police will be out there looking for us.

15:33.480 --> 15:35.300
We don't have much time.

15:35.300 --> 15:37.620
We should decide on our next course of action soon.

15:37.620 --> 15:38.830
Yeah.

15:37.620 --> 15:38.830
Yeah.

15:38.830 --> 15:43.690
You are <i>positive</i> the criminals are from a struggling idol group named Tracy?

15:43.690 --> 15:45.420
Positive! I saw them!

15:45.420 --> 15:46.960
I saw them too!

15:46.960 --> 15:51.780
Those sluts were infatuated with the guy!

15:51.780 --> 15:53.050
Okay.

15:53.050 --> 15:55.460
Put out a search warrant for the three of them.

15:55.460 --> 15:58.940
Phone the media companies and related agencies and ask for their cooperation.

15:58.940 --> 16:01.050
Make sure every jurisdiction is up to speed.

16:01.050 --> 16:03.440
Get permission from headquarters to dispatch a helicopter.

16:02.940 --> 16:03.440
Roger!

16:04.280 --> 16:08.160
So when you said "I've decided" earlier, you meant...

16:08.160 --> 16:10.900
I was going to talk to Taguchi-san face-to-face.

16:10.900 --> 16:13.170
"Please do your job properly.

16:13.170 --> 16:16.140
If that's too much for you, we want a new manager.

16:16.140 --> 16:17.880
And if that's too much still,

16:17.880 --> 16:20.500
you might as well fire us,"
was what I was going to say.

16:21.480 --> 16:25.010
Taguchi would have been furious.

16:25.010 --> 16:28.090
Yeah, but I couldn't find him.

16:28.090 --> 16:30.880
But I still think <i>something</i> had to be said, you know?

16:31.200 --> 16:33.080
Because I...

16:33.080 --> 16:35.510
really love Tracy.

16:37.520 --> 16:38.970
You know...

16:40.160 --> 16:42.730
It's my dream to stand on the Musashino Dome stage

16:43.080 --> 16:46.030
with all the seats around me packed.

16:53.390 --> 16:56.240
I want to be up there with the two of you!

16:57.240 --> 16:58.910
Me too.

16:58.910 --> 17:00.990
I want the three of us to sing together forever.

17:00.990 --> 17:02.420
But right now

17:02.420 --> 17:05.300
we need to do something about this, or they'll arrest us as suspects.

17:05.300 --> 17:07.460
They'll put us behind bars, won't they?

17:07.460 --> 17:10.920
Then we <i>really</i> won't sing together ever again.

17:10.920 --> 17:12.690
I don't want that to happen!

17:12.690 --> 17:14.710
Then what do we do?

17:14.710 --> 17:18.240
What do we do to keep singing together?

17:18.240 --> 17:19.680
I believe...

17:19.680 --> 17:21.010
there is only one answer.

17:25.770 --> 17:27.270
Have you decided?

17:28.630 --> 17:29.500
We'll run!

17:29.500 --> 17:31.820
We'll run for as long as we have to, until one day...

17:31.820 --> 17:34.650
...we'll catch the one who framed us!

17:34.650 --> 17:35.940
I understand.

17:35.940 --> 17:38.080
Then there's no time to lose.

17:38.080 --> 17:39.090
Huh?

17:39.090 --> 17:40.660
Take a look at the internet.

17:41.040 --> 17:43.340
You're the headline of the day.

17:44.200 --> 17:45.870
Look at this! Our follower count...

17:45.880 --> 17:48.120
Alpine brought us pastries and they were so yummy~

17:45.880 --> 17:48.120
—Akane

17:45.880 --> 17:48.120
1 hour ago

17:46.320 --> 17:48.120
It's over 50,000?!

17:48.120 --> 17:50.840
Tracy is trending as well!

17:50.840 --> 17:52.840
We're the top story on Yahooo News <i>too</i>!

17:51.610 --> 17:52.840
Here's why the idol group Tracy is suspected of murder.

17:53.220 --> 17:55.180
And look at all the new views on our PV!

17:55.180 --> 17:56.840
It's at almost one millio—

17:56.840 --> 17:58.220
No, 1.1 million!

18:00.570 --> 18:02.430
Tracy?

18:04.470 --> 18:06.520
Get out of there immediately!

18:06.520 --> 18:08.620
Head towards the park's basement parking.

18:08.620 --> 18:09.240
Is that clear?

18:09.240 --> 18:10.230
Roger!

18:10.230 --> 18:12.250
Got a shot of Tracy running away!

18:12.460 --> 18:12.480
Saba can

18:12.460 --> 18:12.480
Tracy's at the amusement park

18:13.420 --> 18:13.440
Neko-sama

18:13.420 --> 18:13.440
I found the murderer idols!

18:14.360 --> 18:14.400
yukinco Z

18:15.230 --> 18:16.580
Once you're in the parking lot

18:16.580 --> 18:20.100
shut off your phones and any other mobile devices.

18:20.100 --> 18:22.030
The police will already be tracing them!

18:22.030 --> 18:23.180
But...

18:23.180 --> 18:25.060
How will we contact you?

18:25.060 --> 18:28.160
No worries. I've prepared a secure line

18:28.160 --> 18:29.540
along with a means of mobility.

18:32.540 --> 18:34.420
Use the bike and sidecar.

18:34.780 --> 18:37.300
Isn't this too big for us to handle?

18:37.300 --> 18:39.300
I can drive this, no problem!

18:39.300 --> 18:40.410
Alpine?

18:40.410 --> 18:41.550
Seriously?

18:41.550 --> 18:42.530
Yeah.

18:42.530 --> 18:45.400
Before I became an idol,

18:45.400 --> 18:48.390
I was a stunt actor for an action series

18:48.390 --> 18:50.740
called Stink Bug Rider Stinkerton.

18:53.860 --> 18:56.480
My, this bike is so well built.

18:56.480 --> 18:58.730
Wait a minute. That show...

18:58.730 --> 19:00.810
...aired 10 years ago, if I'm not mistaken.

19:00.810 --> 19:03.740
Didn't you say you were 17, Alpine?

19:05.240 --> 19:07.350
The police are surrounding the area.

19:07.350 --> 19:10.250
Take the Aqua-Line out of Tokyo.

19:21.550 --> 19:21.630
Tracy

19:21.550 --> 19:21.630
—Akane

19:21.550 --> 19:21.630
We are going to perform a mini concert and serve food

19:21.550 --> 19:21.630
1 day ago

19:22.010 --> 19:22.050
at the mall tomorrow. Please join us —Aya

19:22.010 --> 19:22.050
Exodus! Now ☆

19:22.010 --> 19:22.050
Just now

19:23.340 --> 19:23.550
Alpine brought us pastries and they were so yummy~

19:23.470 --> 19:23.550
1 hour ago

19:51.820 --> 19:52.830
Don't let them escape!

19:53.160 --> 19:56.760
The criminals took a right on Yanagibashi
and are heading north up Sakae avenue.

19:56.760 --> 19:59.210
I bet they're heading for Oume road.

19:59.500 --> 20:03.670
To all officers in pursuit: you've been cleared for the use of small arms.

20:03.670 --> 20:05.480
They <i>must</i> be stopped!

20:06.180 --> 20:06.220
@jp_tracy_offical My friend has that same bike

20:06.430 --> 20:06.470
A Delivery Guy

20:06.430 --> 20:06.470
@jp_tracy_offical Just comply with the police and surrender

20:06.640 --> 20:06.680
Takao Express Train

20:06.800 --> 20:08.180
Incredible...

20:08.180 --> 20:11.180
Our follower count broke the 300,000 mark.

20:20.030 --> 20:21.360
Alpine! Look!

20:23.950 --> 20:25.030
A gun?

20:31.330 --> 20:33.170
Thanks, mister.

20:36.580 --> 20:37.000
A foreigner is here. Crisis!

20:37.460 --> 20:38.340
Ponokichi

20:37.460 --> 20:38.340
Got a 44 Magnum pistol ! #run_tracy

20:38.340 --> 20:40.360
This route will take them straight to Tokyo Bay.

20:40.360 --> 20:42.470
Then that means their goal is...

20:42.470 --> 20:45.590
Hurry, all troops relocate from the Rainbow Bridge!
Block the Aqua-line!

20:45.590 --> 20:47.480
I want every officer Chiba prefecture has!

20:47.910 --> 20:49.850
This ends in Umihotaru!

21:01.560 --> 21:03.280
That's right, a human wave attack!

21:03.280 --> 21:06.780
They'll never pass an ocean this vast!

21:10.670 --> 21:12.120
Listen, girls...

21:12.790 --> 21:16.190
We're not leaving forever. We'll come back to Tokyo,

21:16.190 --> 21:18.250
to the Musashino Dome!

21:18.250 --> 21:19.420
Yeah!

21:19.420 --> 21:20.800
Right!

21:30.990 --> 21:32.570
Stand your ground, she's bluffing!

21:32.570 --> 21:34.930
A lowly idol doesn't have the wit to fire a gun!

21:34.930 --> 21:37.940
An idol's more determined than you think.

21:45.860 --> 21:48.490
You fools! The Chiba side is closed down!

21:52.740 --> 21:53.700
What?!

21:53.700 --> 21:56.210
Let's go!

22:03.360 --> 22:05.700
Stop!

22:10.700 --> 22:11.680
Who're you?

22:11.680 --> 22:13.420
It's me, who else?

22:13.420 --> 22:14.970
Oh, it's just Aya.

22:14.970 --> 22:16.400
I'm Alpine!

22:16.400 --> 22:18.650
And you're Aya-chan, right?

22:18.650 --> 22:20.440
I'm Akane.

22:20.440 --> 22:24.070
Come to think of it, we've never...

22:24.070 --> 22:26.440
...seen each other without makeup.

22:26.440 --> 22:27.950
Yeppers.

22:41.330 --> 22:43.960
Although this turn of events didn't exactly turn out as planned,

22:43.960 --> 22:47.210
it's interesting in and of itself.

22:50.040 --> 22:51.970
Those bitches...

22:52.200 --> 22:53.520
Tracy...

22:53.520 --> 22:56.970
I'll put you behind bars, I swear it.

22:57.350 --> 23:01.320
And thus, with absolutely zero thought of where to start or where we'll end,

23:01.320 --> 23:03.610
our scanty escape began.

23:04.080 --> 23:09.510
And yet, never in our wildest dreams did we expect...

23:09.510 --> 23:10.490
Don't tell me...

23:13.820 --> 23:14.700
Wait!

23:17.400 --> 23:22.920
that this dramatic escape of ours would cause an uproar so huge it'd last three months and 11 days

23:22.920 --> 23:27.390
and force us to travel over 50,000 kilometers through 12 different countries!

23:52.580 --> 23:56.060
Fluffy, chewy... Oh, what could it be?

23:56.060 --> 23:59.480
So exotic and soft... It sounds like fun!

23:59.480 --> 24:02.910
It's a perfect mystery shining bright

24:02.910 --> 24:08.390
I knew it! That's it! That's what it is!

24:08.890 --> 24:14.640
It starts off A Melody, the malice of a dream

24:15.770 --> 24:22.140
My desires for it grow as it puts me center stage

24:25.240 --> 24:26.940
Right now!

24:28.660 --> 24:30.320
Together!

24:30.320 --> 24:33.700
With matching voice and matching song

24:33.700 --> 24:37.190
it keeps stepping forward

24:37.190 --> 24:42.920
in a fluffy, frilly dream
